supermox-dhcp-client (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Thin alias (crhy/SuperMox#9): the two DHCP answers landed together -
    this package's /usr/sbin/dhclient adapter and pve-container's
    0003-maintained-dhcp-client patch - so they are now one path. The
    patched pve-container path (the container image's own client, run
    through /usr/share/lxc/hooks/pve-dhcp-client) is what pve-container
    calls directly and it needs no host binary, so this package no longer
    ships /usr/sbin/dhclient and instead depends on pve-container.
  * Provides/Replaces/Conflicts: isc-dhcp-client dropped with the adapter:
    the interim isc-dhcp fork stays the only package that can own
    /usr/sbin/dhclient; removing that fork (and its apt pins) is a
    separate decision for rhY, listed in the release notes.

 -- SuperMox <noreply@supermox.me>  Sat, 28 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0800

supermox-dhcp-client (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: /usr/sbin/dhclient (which is /sbin/dhclient on Devuan,
    where /sbin is a symlink to /usr/sbin) as a POSIX sh adapter that
    implements the ISC dhclient command line and the dhclient-script contract
    on top of a maintained DHCP client: dhcpcd by default, udhcpc/udhcpc6 or
    a stand-in through SUPERMOX_DHCP_CLIENT.
  * Provides/Replaces/Conflicts: isc-dhcp-client so pve-container's
    dependency is satisfied without the Debian trixie isc-dhcp fork and
    without re-pinning every upstream security update (crhy/SuperMox#9).
  * Depends: dhcpcd-base | udhcpc | busybox-udhcpc - the clients Devuan
    Ceres actually ships. No ISC source is copied and no systemd is pulled
    in.

 -- SuperMox <noreply@supermox.me>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:30:00 -0700
